id: liquid
name: Liquid
kind: state
description: >
  Amorphous. A Size Category smaller, harder to hold and impossible to Pin, quieter,
  free to move - and unable to attack.
text: >
  (1)-[Passive]: Reduce your Size Category by 1.

  (2)-[Passive]: Increase all of your Grapple Checks made as the Grappled by 1(T) and
  you cannot be Pinned.

  (3)-[Passive]: Increase your Stealth Skill Checks by 2.

  (4)-[Passive]: Your Movement Maneuver does not provoke the Exploit Maneuver.

  (5)-[Passive]: You cannot use any form of Attacking Maneuver or Unique Ability.

  (6)-[1/Round]: As a Standard Action with an Action Cost of 1 Action, you may use a
  Healing Surge.

---

# (1) through (5). Each one is a Slot, and each Slot is read somewhere - which is worth
# saying because four of the five were written for this and a Slot nobody reads is an
# effect that quietly does nothing.
#
# (1) is a step down the list of Size Categories rather than a Size named outright, which
# is how the rules state every move: `size.steps` is settled in the Tier pass, before the
# Size is resolved, so everything a Size decides follows from it - the Defense and Soak
# modifiers, the Melee Range, the Speed, the Squares, and the Skill adjustments. A step
# past the end of the list leaves you at the end of the list.
#
# (2) names a side: the Grappled is always the Defender of a Grapple Check, whoever opened
# it, so `grapple.defending` is read there and nowhere else. A Grapple Check you make as
# the Grappler is a Strike Roll like any other and gets nothing from this.
#
# "You cannot be Pinned" is immunity to the Combat Condition, which is what forbidding the
# Condition itself means here.
#
# (3) is flat, not scaled: "by 2" and not "by 2(T)", which is what the entry says.
#
# (4) is asked where an Exploit is offered, which is the only place one is ever offered
# from. Nothing here watches a token leave a Melee Range, so this does not have to: what it
# stops is the card handing the opening out.
[passive]
size.steps -= 1;
grapple.defending += 1(T);
forbid condition.pinned;
skill.stealth.bonus += 2;
forbid movement.provokes;
forbid attackingManeuvers;
forbid uniqueAbilities;

# --- (6), which is said and not built ---------------------------------------------------
#
# "As a Standard Action with an Action Cost of 1 Action, you may use a Healing Surge",
# once a Combat Round.
#
# Written as an effect it would be `[1/round, costs 1 action]` with a Healing Surge in it,
# and that block would compile and never run: an effect is collected by the Moment it names
# and this one names none, so nothing would ever look for it. The `costs` keyword is parsed
# and spent by nobody as well - Pinned and Prone both write it, and neither takes the
# Action - so even a block that did fire would be free.
#
# So it is said rather than half-built. The Surge machinery is all there and the table can
# use it; what is missing is the door, which is a Maneuver this entry does not name and
# this system will not invent.
